From: Joan Karadimov <joan.karadimov@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] There is no root to refuse on Windows

geteuid() does not exist in mingw-w64, and this is the only thing in the
header that needs it -- 65 of the 185 errors in an unpatched Windows build
come from this one line reaching 65 translation units.

false is not a stub, it is the answer. Every caller of isRootRunning() is a
gate that turns the tool away when it is true ("cannot run as root", exit
-4), and on MSYS2 nobody is root.

Not for upstream: only correct where root does not exist.
diff --git a/src/unixcommand.h b/src/unixcommand.h
index c0c4569..6230a47 100644
--- a/src/unixcommand.h
+++ b/src/unixcommand.h
@@ -118,8 +118,15 @@ public:
   static bool isOctoToolRunning(const QString &octoToolName);
 
   static bool isRootRunning(){
+#ifdef Q_OS_WIN
+    // MSYS2 has no root. pacman writes to an installation the invoking user
+    // already owns, so there is nothing to escalate to and nothing to refuse:
+    // every caller of this is a gate that turns octopi away when it is true.
+    return false;
+#else
     int uid = geteuid();
     return (uid == 0); //Returns TRUE if root is running Octopi
+#endif
   }
 
   static bool isUserInWheelGroup();
